<%# On shared/_table_container, like every other table in the app.

    This was a hand-rolled `overflow-x-auto` div, so measured on a Chromebook the grades table sat on
    **no surface at all**: 0px border, transparent background, 0px radius, against a slate-50 page. The
    roster on classrooms#show had exactly this defect and design.md records it as fixed there.

    region_label keeps the keyboard-scroll affordance the hand-rolled version was written for: a
    scrolling container needs to be focusable or its right-hand columns are unreachable without a mouse
    (axe scrollable-region-focusable). It is a container option now rather than a reason to bypass the
    container.

    The Earns column is the trailing one, so it right-aligns with tabular-nums and the figures line up
    down the column - which is also why nothing else goes in those cells. The <tfoot> carries the
    subtotals and the total: see _earnings_footer for why they belong to the table rather than to a card
    of their own. %>
<% earnings = grade_book_earnings %>

<%# table-stacked: below lg this stops being a grid and each student becomes a block of labelled
    fields. A table of inputs cannot use the collapse the other tables use, because restating a control
    in the primary cell would submit two inputs with the same name. See tables.css. %>
<%= render "shared/table_container", region_label: "Grades", table_class: "table-stacked" do %>
  <thead>
    <tr class="table-header-row">
      <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left">Student</th>
      <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left">Math</th>
      <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left">Reading</th>
      <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left">Days attended</th>
      <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-left">Perfect attendance</th>
      <th scope="col" class="table-header-cell table-header-cell-right">Earns</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>

  <tbody class="bg-white">
    <%= render partial: "grade_entry",
               collection: grade_book.grade_entries.sort_by { it.user.display_name.to_s },
               as: :entry,
               locals: { disabled: grade_book.completed?, grade_book_earnings: earnings } %>
  </tbody>

  <%= render "earnings_footer", earnings: earnings %>
<% end %>
